{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 3's LLM-Review found a genuine blocking correctness bug: candidate_verdict_flip discarded stored_blocking_criteria whenever candidate_findings was empty (a normal outcome, not an error) -- under-counting relieved criteria for any row where the candidate legitimately produced nothing. Fixed: compute stored_blocking unconditionally, only short-circuit the verify/decide call. Also fixed a test that had been (accidentally) encoding the bug as correct behavior, and added coverage for the 2 non-blocking advisory findings from the same review pass (_exclude_det_findings mixed-criteria single-finding case; cleanup_reconstructed_ticket's worktree-remove-failure fallback. 36/36 unit tests passing, lint/format/typecheck clean. Pushed as patchset 4 on change 2450.\nEOF\n)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788229625714158001,"uuid":"a67fe4df-53fb-41b2-a793-64bd2e5ecbec"}